---
import Book from '../../layouts/Book.astro';
import {lessons,label,decisionPath,decisionLessons,timeEstimate,timeModel,formatMinutes,render,FT_MODULE,completePathLessons} from '../../lib/content';
const route=decisionLessons();
const rows=await Promise.all(route.map(async l=>({lesson:l,time:await timeEstimate(l),callout:(await render(decisionPath.callouts[l.id]??'')).html})));
const total=rows.reduce((t,r)=>t+r.time.total,0);
const algorithmRows=rows.filter(r=>r.lesson.module!==FT_MODULE),ftRows=rows.filter(r=>r.lesson.module===FT_MODULE);
const stageMinutes=(list:typeof rows)=>list.reduce((t,r)=>t+r.time.total,0);
const main=completePathLessons();
const mainTotal=(await Promise.all(main.map(l=>timeEstimate(l)))).reduce((t,e)=>t+e.total,0);
const sections=[{id:'the-chain',title:'The chain this path follows'},{id:'algorithm-stage',title:'Stage 1: algorithms'},{id:'error-correction-stage',title:'Stage 2: error correction'},{id:'time-estimates',title:'How time is estimated'}];
---
<Book title="Decision path" sections={sections} tocLabel="ON THIS PAGE"><span class="eyebrow">THE DEFAULT ROUTE</span><h1>{decisionPath.title}</h1><p class="dek">{decisionPath.summary}</p>
<div class="context-box"><p><strong>Who this is for.</strong> Readers deciding what quantum computing means for a business or a career, who need to follow a published resource estimate from the application down to hardware and judge it.</p><p><strong>Length so far:</strong> {route.length} lessons, about {formatMinutes(total)} by the time model below: {algorithmRows.length} algorithm lessons ({formatMinutes(stageMinutes(algorithmRows))}) and {ftRows.length} error-correction lessons ({formatMinutes(stageMinutes(ftRows))}). </p><p>Want every algorithm family instead? The <a href="/path/complete/">complete algorithms path</a> has {main.length} lessons, about {formatMinutes(mainTotal)}.</p></div>
<div class="prose">
<h2 id="the-chain">The chain this path follows</h2>
<ol><li><strong>What a useful application needs:</strong> logical qubits, T or Toffoli count, runtime.</li><li><strong>Error-correction overhead:</strong> code distance, physical qubits per logical qubit, magic-state supply.</li><li><strong>What the infrastructure must deliver:</strong> decoder throughput and latency, control channels, calibration.</li><li><strong>Hardware modalities and roadmaps.</strong></li><li><strong>A realistic timeline to usefulness.</strong></li></ol>
<p>Each lesson on this path opens with a short note on why it matters for that chain. Lessons are also labelled by tier everywhere on the site: <em>Decision path</em>, <em>Complete path</em>, or <em>Deferred branch</em> (read after the decision path).</p>
<h2 id="algorithm-stage">Stage 1: algorithms</h2>
</div>
<ol class="catalog-list decision-list">{algorithmRows.map(({lesson,time,callout},i)=><li data-decision-step={i+1}><a href={`/lessons/${lesson.id}/`}>{label(lesson)}</a><p>{lesson.summary}</p><div class="small decision-why" set:html={callout}/><p class="path-minutes">About {time.total} min: {time.reading} reading + {time.calculation} calculation</p></li>)}</ol>
<div class="prose">
<p>Lessons 25 and 26 are on this path because lesson 27 lists them as prerequisites. Lesson 25 underpins the chemistry estimates, and lesson 26 explains why a solver's output is a quantum state rather than printed numbers.</p>
<h2 id="error-correction-stage">Stage 2: error correction and fault tolerance</h2>
<p>The module "FT: Error correction and fault tolerance" covers errors and the surface code, decoding and its real-time constraints, magic states, the control stack, end-to-end resource estimation, and hardware roadmaps. It ends with the synthesis page, "The full chain", which runs one workload from application to timeline with the resource calculator. Every lesson listed below is published.</p>
</div><ol class="catalog-list decision-list">{ftRows.map(({lesson,time,callout},i)=><li data-decision-step={algorithmRows.length+i+1}><a href={`/lessons/${lesson.id}/`}>{label(lesson)}</a><p>{lesson.summary}</p><div class="small decision-why" set:html={callout}/><p class="path-minutes">About {time.total} min: {time.reading} reading + {time.calculation} calculation</p></li>)}</ol>
<div class="prose">
<h2 id="time-estimates">How time is estimated</h2>
<p>Reading time is the rendered lesson text at {timeModel.wordsPerMinute} words per minute. Calculation time adds {timeModel.perDisplayEquation} minutes per display equation, {timeModel.perCheck} minutes per in-lesson prediction or derivation block, and {timeModel.perPractice} minutes per practice question. These constants are editorial estimates, not measurements of real readers. Time yourself on lessons 01 and 11 and scale the totals.</p>
</div>
</Book>
